  "id": "Compound::DB01403 - Gene::152",
  "verbalization": "Methotrimeprazine is likely to interact with Adra2c through a mechanism involving the Alpha-adrenergic receptor pathway. The evidence suggests that Methotrimeprazine binds to Adra1d, which then participates in Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, ultimately leading to Adra2c being part of this activity. This implies a potential role for Methotrimeprazine in modulating Adra2c function via the adrenergic receptor system. The consistent binding to Adra1d across multiple paths, coupled with the shared participation in Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, supports a unified mechanism where Methotrimeprazine influences Adra2c through the adrenergic receptor pathway. The evidence is robust, but the exact nature of the interaction remains somewhat indirect, as the pathways are mediated through intermediate receptors and activities.",
